  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An ancient Celtiberian settlement located just west of the modern town of Caminreal in Spain's Teruel province. The settlement flourished between the second and first centuries BCE and, having been destroyed or abandoned, was succeeded by the settlement at Cerro de San Esteban. ",
